\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Every version of the skill. Differences in $p$ are paired by text with 95\% bootstrap intervals; rank differences for v12 and v13 are differences in mean rank, bootstrapped over briefs; positive means the row's version ranked better. v1--v4 rows: personal-statement pairwise judgments of better writing in development (skill wins : plain wins; four judgments per row), with unsupported claims summed over the same pairs. v3--v4 used depth notes (the student's answers to the skill's depth questions); v4 on the original notes went 1:1 with 4 vs 14 unsupported claims; v1--v2 used the original notes, where unsupported claims were 16 vs 29 and 6 vs 33. Content hashes (Section~\ref {sec:bench} says which were recorded before testing): v8 8fe68e27a7a0e007, v9 6e56b690fba3cd03, v10 d05f855dc7111b57, v10.1 3571b11768657399, v11 cdda4484b09a1155, v12 0fd7410cda39fa06, v13 5e5db96e61ff8552.}}{15}{table.caption.40}\protected@file@percent }
